=begin rakudoc
=head1 Standalone Functions

The functions mentioned here are the same as the methods explained in B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-BitsetIter> except that the name is longer. See also L<.init-first()|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gtk4/N-BitsetIter.html#init-first>, L<.init-last()|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gtk4/N-BitsetIter.html#init-last> or L<.init-at() all defined in package Gnome::Gtk4::N-BitsetIter|/content-docs/api2/reference/Gtk4/N-BitsetIter.html#init-at>.

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 bitset-iter-init-at

Initializes C<$iter> to point to C<$target>.

If C<$target> is not found, finds the next value after it. If no value >= C<$target> exists in C<$set>, this function returns C<False>.

=begin code
method bitset-iter-init-at (
  N-Object $iter, N-Object $set, UInt() $target, Array[Int] $value
  --> Bool
)
=end code

=item $iter; a pointer to an uninitialized B<Gnome::Gtk4::T-bitset>
=item $set; a B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-Bitset>
=item $target; target value to start iterating at.
=item $value; (transfer ownership: full) Set to the found value in C<$set>.

Return value; C<True> if a value was found.

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 bitset-iter-init-first

Initializes an iterator for C<$set> and points it to the first value in C<$set>.

If C<$set> is empty, C<False> is returned and C<$value> is set to C<G_MAXUINT>.

=begin code
method bitset-iter-init-first (
  N-Object $iter, N-Object $set, Array[Int] $value
  --> Bool
)
=end code

=item $iter; a pointer to an uninitialized B<Gnome::Gtk4::T-bitset>
=item $set; a B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-Bitset>
=item $value; (transfer ownership: full) Set to the first value in C<$set>.

Return value; C<True> if C<$set> isn't empty.

=end rakudoc

#-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
=begin rakudoc
=head2 bitset-iter-init-last

Initializes an iterator for C<$set> and points it to the last value in C<$set>.

If C<$set> is empty, C<False> is returned.

=begin code
method bitset-iter-init-last (
  N-Object $iter, N-Object $set, Array[Int] $value
  --> Bool
)
=end code

=item $iter; a pointer to an uninitialized B<Gnome::Gtk4::T-bitset>
=item $set; a B<Gnome::Gtk4::N-Bitset>
=item $value; (transfer ownership: full) Set to the last value in C<$set>.

Return value; C<True> if C<$set> isn't empty.

=end rakudoc

